  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "style": "NewsLabel",
      "text": "FICTIONAL COMMUNITY ISSUE / ORIGINAL EDITORIAL SPECIMEN"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "THE COMMON PAPER"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsDeck",
      "text": "Neighbourhood ideas, clear sources and visible corrections"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsIssue",
      "text": "ISSUE 01 • OCTOBER 2026 • TWO-PAGE DEMONSTRATION"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsLabel",
      "text": "PROPOSALS / NEIGHBOURHOOD INFORMATION"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "A proposal for one shared noticeboard"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsDeck",
      "text": "A fictional neighbourhood considers how a small public board could carry details that readers can check."
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsNote",
      "text": "Studio Templates | Original fictional report | Sources N1 and C1"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsNote",
      "text": "AI-generated fictional streetscape. Illustration only; not a photograph of a real neighbourhood or…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Putting notices in one place is only the first step. The proposal supplied with this issue asks what…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Under the proposed rule, every notice would identify its organiser, intended audience, current status…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "An earlier specimen described the board as opening this month. That wording was stronger than the…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The next step is to establish a responsible editor and a way to verify each notice with its organiser.…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "A small rule with a clear owner"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "A useful notice names the person or group responsible for its facts. An editor can improve wording, but…"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsLabel",
      "text": "READER’S DESK"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Before you act on a notice"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Use these questions to check a draft. This issue does not supply a real event or sign-up route."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "Who owns the information?"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Look for the named organiser and a verified way to ask a question. A publication title is not a…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "What is its status?"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Separate an idea, a proposal and a confirmed arrangement. Do not infer approval from polished…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "What could have changed?"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Check the latest version and update date. If time, place, cost or access is unresolved, ask the…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "Can a correction be found?"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "A correction should identify the earlier item and explain the change. Page 2 demonstrates one…"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsIssue",
      "text": "IN THIS SPECIMEN 2 proposals / 0 approved events 1 documented wording correction"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsNote",
      "text": "These counts describe the supplied editorial fixtures only. They are not a survey, attendance measure…"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsLabel",
      "text": "THE COMMON PAPER / EDITORIAL NOTEBOOK"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "What needs checking next"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsDeck",
      "text": "Two short articles connect the proposals to sources, ownership and practical next steps."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "A repair corner is still a proposal"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsNote",
      "text": "Original fictional report | Source N2"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "A second brief proposes a small conversation about caring for everyday objects. It does not announce a…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The distinction matters for the notice. A discussion about a possible activity should ask what needs to…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Before a real invitation is written, the organiser would need to confirm the activity, responsible…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "The question for the next draft"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "What exactly is being offered, by whom, and with what confirmed limits? Answer those questions from the…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "Keep the update with the story"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsNote",
      "text": "Editorial practice | Sources N1, N2 and C1"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "A clear correction is part of the information service. Readers should be able to find the affected…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The correction below concerns wording in this original specimen. The earlier notice implied an opening…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "For a real issue, retain the earlier version in an editorial record, publish the correction beside a…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "A practical reading action"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Compare the corrected sentence with source N1. Then name one fact that would still need verification…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Correction record"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsLabel",
      "text": "C1 / ORIGINAL FICTIONAL NOTICE / VERSION 1 → VERSION 2 / RECORD DATE: 1 OCTOBER 2026"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsNote",
      "text": "This is a demonstrated correction to original fictional text, not a correction issued by a real…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading3",
      "text": "Source desk and permissions"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsNote",
      "text": "N1: source-records.json / noticeboard proposal. N2: source-records.json / repair-corner proposal. C1:…"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsNote",
      "text": "No interviews, personal testimony, real event details or measured outcomes are claimed. The…"
    },
    {
      "style": "NewsLabel",
      "text": "FICTIONAL DEMONSTRATION • THE COMMON PAPER"
    }
